# Page objects

Follow `@src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/LoginPage.java`, `@src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/SuccessfulLoginPage.java`, and `@src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/BasePage.java`. For elements that appear after a click, follow `@src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/ExceptionsPage.java`. For a filter, sort, menu, or table, follow `@src/main/java/com/practicetestautomation/pageobjects/TablePage.java`.

- Package `com.practicetestautomation.pageobjects`. `public class <Name>Page extends BasePage`.
- Constructor only calls `super(driver)`. Use `driver` and `wait` from `BasePage`. Do not construct a `WebDriver` or `WebDriverWait`.
- Import `By`, `WebDriver`, and `WebElement` only when used. No `PageFactory` or `@FindBy`.
- Locator fields are `private static final By`, suffix `Locator`, and they sit before the constructor. Prefer `By.id`. Use `By.linkText` for a link. Scope an xpath to one group when an id repeats, as `TablePage` scopes a radio to its fieldset legend.
- Do not build a `By` inside a method. Do not concatenate a parameter into a CSS or XPath string.
- A fixed set of choices is a public enum on the page. Each constant holds one complete `By` literal. Public methods take that enum. They do not take a markup value (`data-value`, option `value`, column name) as a `String`.
- A public method does not return `By` or `WebElement`. Return a collection with `List.copyOf`.

## Actions

- `visit()` calls `super.visit` with this page's address. Omit `visit()` when another page opens this one, as `SuccessfulLoginPage` does.
- Names: `click...`, `enter...(String)`, `select...(Enum)`, `get...` for text, `is...Displayed` for a check, `load` to wait for a landmark.
- Return `void`, `String`, `boolean`, a value type, or the next page (`new SuccessfulLoginPage(driver)`).
- A typing method takes the text as an argument. Do not store credentials or expected messages.
- Do not assert. The locator a method uses is the element its name describes.
- Skip the click when a radio, checkbox, or `<select>` is already in the requested state. Click a toggling control, such as a menu button with `aria-expanded`, only when it is closed.
- A native `<select>` uses `org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select` and `selectByValue`. A custom menu is not a `Select`.
- Read an input's current value with `getDomProperty`. Read `data-*` and `aria-*` with `getDomAttribute`. Do not call `getAttribute`.
- A number parsed from visible text: remove commas and spaces only, then `Integer.parseInt` the whole remainder. The exception includes the original text. Do not delete every non-digit.

## Waits

Use the `BasePage` helpers. Add a new shared wait there instead of copying one. After an action, wait for the resulting state on the `wait` field (`elementToBeSelected`, `elementSelectionStateToBe`, `attributeToBe`, `textToBe`). Do not construct another `WebDriverWait`.

- Element is already on the page, and this method does not follow an action that changes it: `driver.findElement(locator)`.
- Field may already hold text: `clear()`, then `sendKeys`. Otherwise `sendKeys` only.
- Text that appears later: `waitForElement(locator).getText()`.
- Click once enabled: `waitForElementToBeClickable(locator).click()`.
- Landmark for `load()` or `visit()`: `waitForElement(locator)`.
- Visible now, unchanged by this method: `isDisplayed(locator)`.
- Becomes visible: `waitForIsDisplayed(locator)`, named `is...DisplayedAfterWait`.
- Goes away: `waitForInvisibilityOfElement`, named `is...NoLongerDisplayedAfterWait`.
- Read a message's text only after `waitForElement`. Check that it is gone with `waitForInvisibilityOfElement`. Do not pair `isDisplayed` with `waitForElement` for the same message.
